[
    {
        "content": "<p>Just for future reference for Physlib, what is Mathlib's policies (if any) on having a company as the copyright holder of a file e.g. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Copyright</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2025</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyMadeUpCompany</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">All</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rights</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reserved</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Released</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">under</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Apache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">2.0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">license</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">described</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LICENSE</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Authors</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I <a href=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aleanprover-community%2Fmathlib4%20Concordance%20Inc.%20dba%20Harmonic.&amp;type=code\">see</a> that there are some of these for Harmonic, but it seems like they are few and far between.</p>",
        "id": 594295580,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1778506081
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are also 27 files with Lean FRO, and 1 with Google (<a href=\"https://tqft.net/mathlib4files/Data/List/Palindrome\">file#Data/List/Palindrome</a>)</p>",
        "id": 594297497,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1778506476
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the practical policy is \"if the original author could plausibly say that the initial copyright should belong to that entity, and that they are authorized by the entity to do the release under the apache license, then everything is fine\". (And in particular that is implicitly plausible for any identifiable employee of an identifiable company.)</p>",
        "id": 594297962,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1778506576
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The Google one seems to contain some relevant lore: see <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110031\">Patrick Massot</span>'s review in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/pull/3729\">!3#3729</a></p>",
        "id": 594299857,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1778506986
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Makes sense! Thank you both. Thanks for the link <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"933054\">@Snir Broshi</span></p>",
        "id": 594300725,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1778507165
    }
]